CAT = "nzsecLicensing"; SEG = "LIC"
Q = [
('A security company that provides guards for money must hold:',
 'A company licence', ['An individual licence', 'A certificate of approval', 'A liquor licence'],
 'The PSPLA issues company licences to companies that provide private security services for money. Each staff member doing the work then needs a current COA.'),
('A guard employed by a licensed security company needs:',
 'A certificate of approval', ['A company licence of their own', 'An individual licence', 'No approval of their own'],
 "A COA is for employees and contractors of a licence holder. The company's licence does not cover the people it sends out to do the work."),
('A sole trader who guards building sites for money needs:',
 'An individual licence', ['A certificate of approval', 'A company licence', 'Only a first aid certificate'],
 'A person working for themselves, not for a licence holder, needs an individual licence. A COA is only for someone employed or engaged by a licence holder.'),
('Which class of work covers checking who enters a venue and removing people?',
 'Crowd controller', ['Property guard', 'Personal guard', 'Monitoring officer'],
 'The PSPLA describes crowd controllers as people who check who enters premises or events, keep order and remove people: bouncers, door and event security.'),
('Guarding a site and responding to its alarm callouts falls under which class?',
 'Property guard', ['Crowd controller', 'Security technician', 'Security consultant'],
 'Property guards guard property and respond to alarm callouts on site. A security technician installs or repairs devices rather than guarding.'),
('A bodyguard protecting a visiting performer works in which class?',
 'Personal guard', ['Property guard', 'Crowd controller', 'Private investigator'],
 'The personal guard class covers protecting people, such as bodyguards.'),
('A control-room officer who watches alarms off site and never attends callouts is a:',
 'Monitoring officer', ['Property guard', 'Crowd controller', 'Security consultant'],
 'The monitoring officer class covers monitoring systems remotely off site without responding to callouts. It sits outside the guard minimum training.'),
('A bartender who only makes drinks and clears tables:',
 'Does not need a COA', ['Needs a crowd controller COA', 'Needs a property guard COA', 'Needs a temporary COA'],
 'The PSPLA says bar staff need a COA only if their job includes screening entry, keeping order or removing people. Making drinks and clearing tables is not crowd control.'),
('A bar manager whose duties include removing unruly patrons needs:',
 'A crowd controller COA', ['No approval while on the bar', 'A property guard COA', "Only the duty manager's certificate"],
 'Removing people is crowd control work. The PSPLA says bar staff who screen entry, keep order or remove people as part of their job need a COA.'),
('Which minimum training applies before a property guard COA is granted?',
 'Standards 40146, 40145 and 40147', ['Unit standards 4646 and 16705', 'A workplace first aid certificate', 'A defensive driving course'],
 'The PSPLA accepts skill standards 40146, 40145 and 40147, or unit standards 27364, 27360 and 27361 that they replaced. 4646 and 16705 make up the licence controller qualification for bars.'),
('You start a guarding job before finishing your training. What lets you work?',
 'A temporary certificate', ["Your employer's licence", 'A letter from your trainer', 'An NZQA enrolment slip'],
 'A temporary COA lets a crowd controller, property guard or personal guard work while completing the training.'),
('A temporary certificate of approval lasts:',
 '3 months', ['6 months', '12 months', '4 weeks'],
 'The PSPLA says a temporary COA lasts 3 months. If training is not finished by then, the holder must apply for another one.'),
('Training is finished but your temporary COA has weeks to run. What next?',
 'Upload your record of achievement', ['Wait for the temporary COA to end', 'Sit a PSPLA written exam', 'Send your certificate to Police'],
 'Once training is done you upload your NZQA record of achievement to the PSPLA with your badge number and address, and get a new badge to replace the temporary one.'),
('When you renew a COA, the minimum training:',
 'Does not have to be repeated', ['Must be completed again', 'Must be repeated every second renewal', 'Must be refreshed after 12 months'],
 'The PSPLA says training only has to be completed once and does not need repeating at renewal.'),
('Your home address changes. What must you do?',
 'Tell the PSPLA', ['Tell only your employer', 'Wait until you renew', 'Get a new ID badge printed'],
 'COA holders must tell the Authority when their name or home address changes, or when they are no longer eligible.'),
('You lose your COA ID badge. What do you do?',
 'Apply to the PSPLA for a new one', ['Make a copy to wear in the meantime', "Borrow a colleague's badge", 'Carry your driver licence instead'],
 'A lost badge, licence or certificate is replaced by applying to the PSPLA for a substitute.'),
('You want to add the crowd controller class to your property guard COA. You:',
 'Apply to the PSPLA to add it', ['Start the work straight away', 'Ask your employer to approve it', 'Apply for a company licence'],
 'A class of work is added by sending the PSPLA its add or remove a class form. Until it is added you are not approved for that class.'),
('While working, a COA holder must wear the ID badge:',
 'Where it is readily visible', ['Inside a jacket pocket or wallet', 'Only when a patron asks', 'Only at licensed premises'],
 "Section 67 of the Act requires certificate holders, other than private investigators, to wear the Authority's ID in a readily visible position while working."),
('Which detail is NOT on the PSPLA identification badge?',
 "The holder's name", ["The holder's photo", 'The classes of work', 'The expiry date'],
 'Section 68 lists a unique identifier, photo, classes of work and expiry date. The badge carries no name; the number links to the public register.'),
('A crowd controller covers the number on the ID badge with tape. This:',
 'Breaches the Act', ['Is allowed at night', 'Is fine if the photo shows', "Is allowed with the owner's consent"],
 'In [2023] NZPSPLA 041 the Authority held that every required detail must stay visible. Taping over the number breaches s 67 and may be misconduct.'),
('A patron you are refusing entry asks to see your certificate. You must:',
 'Produce it', ['Refuse if you feel unsafe', 'Tell them to ask Police', "Show only your employer's card"],
 'Section 66 requires a certificate holder to produce the certificate on demand to anyone they deal with while working. There is no safety exemption.'),
('A guard may leave the ID badge off only when wearing it would:',
 "Really threaten someone's safety", ['Spoil the look of the uniform', 'Slow down the door queue', 'Show their number to angry patrons'],
 "Section 67(4) excuses a holder who reasonably believes wearing the badge would threaten their or another's safety. The Authority said the threat must be real or significant."),
('An event steward who only scans tickets and shows people to seats:',
 'Is not doing crowd control', ['Needs a crowd controller COA', 'Needs a temporary COA', 'Must hold a company licence'],
 'Checking that admission has been paid is excluded from crowd control. Stewards are not expected to search, intervene physically or evict.'),
('A guard on a blue temporary COA should be given:',
 'Supervised duties only', ['Solo night patrols', 'High-risk door work', 'Sole charge of a large site'],
 'The NZSA guidelines say staff on a blue temporary COA should only do supervised duties and should not work alone or on higher-risk work.'),
]
